From: Ziy engine fork <ziy@ziy.app>
Date: 2026-10-15
Subject: [PATCH 0003] WebGPU: empty the adapter-identity strings under RFP

Ziy's farbling contract is Brave's, and Brave's WebGPU farbling
(third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu_adapter.cc:
BraveScrubWebGpuAdapterInfo, recon recorded at replica/re-deep-shields.md §5 row
17, brave-webcompat-webgpu) empties `GPUAdapterInfo.vendor`, `.architecture`,
`.device` and `.description` so the GPU name, device class and driver build stop
identifying the machine.

Gecko has no equivalent. `GPUAdapterInfo` (dom/webidl/WebGPU.webidl:71-88)
already ships `vendor`/`architecture`/`device`/`description` as permanently
empty strings -- dom/webgpu/Adapter.h:60-63 -- but the four non-standard
[ChromeOnly] getters that carry the real wgpu-native values are NOT guarded by
any RFPTarget:

  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:83   GetWgpuName()        <- s = mAboutSupportInfo->name
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:91   GetWgpuDeviceType()  <- the disjoint Cpu/DiscreteGpu/... switch
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:114  GetWgpuDriver()      <- s = mAboutSupportInfo->driver
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:118  GetWgpuDriverInfo()  <- s = mAboutSupportInfo->driver_info

Gecko's entire RFP coverage for WebGPU is the three targets
WebGPULimits (Adapter.cpp:332), WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter (Adapter.cpp:73) and
WebGPUSubgroupSizes (Adapter.cpp:39 and :62) -- plus WebGLRenderInfo on the WebGL
side -- and none of them reaches these getters. The per-target override pref
cannot express the fix either: in RFP mode
nsRFPService::IsRFPEnabledFor() (nsRFPService.cpp:335) returns true for every
target before it consults the override set, exactly as 0001 documented for
CSSPrefersColorScheme.

This patch empties all four strings when RFP is active for the adapter's
document. It deliberately does NOT add a new RFPTarget to RFPTargets.inc: doing
that would change the meaning of the target string Ziy locks
("+AllTargets,-CSSPrefersColorScheme") and would require the same
CreateOverridesFromText (nsRFPService.cpp:2685) edit path 0001 avoided. Instead
it reuses the engine's existing WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter target -- the one Gecko
itself already uses for "Always report hardware support for WebGPU" at
Adapter.cpp:73, which is the same decision this patch is making -- so a build
with the gate off is stock Gecko and the shipped pref string remains valid.

Scope note, stated plainly: `vendor`/`architecture`/`device`/`description` (the
standard, web-exposed attributes) are ALREADY empty in stock Gecko, so this
patch changes only the wgpu* attributes, which are reachable from privileged and
chrome code and, per the fingerprinting-surface warning at Adapter.h:56-58, are
exactly the values a WebGPU fingerprinting surface would want to scrub.

Shape note: each `#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING` wraps the whole function body
and the `#endif` is glued to the original first statement with no blank line, so
stripping the gate from the patched file yields a file BYTE-IDENTICAL to
pristine. That is the gate-off proof patches/README.md step 6 requires, verified
by the strip-and-cmp in replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md.

STATUS: authored and apply-verified (git apply --check, git apply,
git apply --reverse --check, and a real reverse followed by cmp against
pristine, all RC=0 -- see replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md). NOT COMPILED: the
first compilation is the first CI run of
.github/workflows/build-gecko.yml.

Gated behind MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING, set by the
--enable-ziy-fingerprinting configure option declared in
0002-ziy-fingerprinting-option.patch. Applies cleanly after 0001 and 0002.

Sources for every claim in this commit message:
  dom/webidl/WebGPU.webidl:71-88 GPUAdapterInfo (vendor/architecture/device/
    description as empty strings; wgpu* the [ChromeOnly] strings)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.h:60-63 GetVendor/GetArchitecture/GetDevice/
    GetDescription -- all `s = nsString()`
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.h:56-58 the "increases fingerprinting surface" warning
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:83 GetWgpuName (unguarded)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:91 GetWgpuDeviceType (unguarded switch)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:114 GetWgpuDriver (unguarded)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:118 GetWgpuDriverInfo (unguarded)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:332 WebGPULimits clamp
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:73 WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter (reused as the gate)
  dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp:39,:62 WebGPUSubgroupSizes
  toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp:335
    IsRFPEnabledFor's RFP short-circuit
  brave-core third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu_adapter.cc:
    BraveScrubWebGpuAdapterInfo (Brave behaviour contract, cited via
    replica/re-deep-shields.md §5 row 17)
---
--- a/dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp
+++ b/dom/webgpu/Adapter.cpp
@@ -81,6 +81,42 @@
 }
 
 void AdapterInfo::GetWgpuName(nsString& s) const {
+#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
+  // Ziy delta 3: the WebGPU adapter-identity strings RFP never reaches.
+  //
+  // WHY A C++ CHANGE IS REQUIRED. Brave's farbling contract for WebGPU
+  // (replica/re-deep-shields.md §5 row 17, brave-webcompat-webgpu,
+  // third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/gpu_adapter.cc:
+  // BraveScrubWebGpuAdapterInfo) empties `adapter.info.vendor` / `.architecture`
+  // / `.device` so the GPU name and driver strings stop identifying the machine.
+  // Gecko has no equivalent. Its RFP coverage for WebGPU is four targets only —
+  // WebGPULimits (Adapter.cpp:332), WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter (Adapter.cpp:73),
+  // WebGPUSubgroupSizes (Adapter.cpp:39 and :62), and WebGLRenderInfo for the
+  // WebGL side — and none of them guards the four DOMString getters on
+  // GPUAdapterInfo that carry the raw wgpu-native values. The per-target
+  // override pref cannot express this either: in RFP mode
+  // nsRFPService::IsRFPEnabledFor() (nsRFPService.cpp:335) returns true for every
+  // target before it consults the override set, and adding a new RFPTarget for
+  // it would mean an RFPTargets.inc edit that the shipped pref string already
+  // assumes is complete. This is the "behaviour the RFP pref layer cannot
+  // express" class of delta, the same one 0001-rfp-colorscheme-carveout patched.
+  //
+  // The gate reuses the engine's own WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter target rather than
+  // introducing a new enum value, so the pref string Ziy locks
+  // ("+AllTargets,-CSSPrefersColorScheme") stays valid and a user could relax
+  // this with --disable or by removing the term. When RFP is off the getters are
+  // byte-for-byte the engine's own behaviour.
+  //
+  // Note the shape: the #ifdef wraps the WHOLE body and the #endif is glued to
+  // the original first statement with no blank line, so stripping the block
+  // leaves a file byte-identical to pristine — the gate-off proof
+  // patches/README.md step 6 requires.
+  if (GetParentObject()->ShouldResistFingerprinting(
+          RFPTarget::WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter)) {
+    s.Truncate();
+    return;
+  }
+#endif  // MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
   s = mAboutSupportInfo->name;
 }
 
@@ -89,6 +125,15 @@
 uint32_t AdapterInfo::WgpuDevice() const { return mAboutSupportInfo->device; }
 
 void AdapterInfo::GetWgpuDeviceType(nsString& s) const {
+#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
+  // Ziy delta 3b: same gap. The device type leaks discrete-vs-integrated GPU.
+  // See the block above GetWgpuName for why the pref layer cannot reach it.
+  if (GetParentObject()->ShouldResistFingerprinting(
+          RFPTarget::WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter)) {
+    s.Truncate();
+    return;
+  }
+#endif  // MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
   switch (mAboutSupportInfo->device_type) {
     case ffi::WGPUDeviceType_Cpu:
       s.AssignLiteral("Cpu");
@@ -112,10 +157,27 @@
 }
 
 void AdapterInfo::GetWgpuDriver(nsString& s) const {
+#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
+  // Ziy delta 3c: the driver string, e.g. "Mesa Intel(R) UHD Graphics 620"
+  // with a driver version. See the block above GetWgpuName for the reasoning.
+  if (GetParentObject()->ShouldResistFingerprinting(
+          RFPTarget::WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter)) {
+    s.Truncate();
+    return;
+  }
+#endif  // MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
   s = mAboutSupportInfo->driver;
 }
 
 void AdapterInfo::GetWgpuDriverInfo(nsString& s) const {
+#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
+  // Ziy delta 3d: the driver-info string. See the block above GetWgpuName.
+  if (GetParentObject()->ShouldResistFingerprinting(
+          RFPTarget::WebGPUIsFallbackAdapter)) {
+    s.Truncate();
+    return;
+  }
+#endif  // MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
   s = mAboutSupportInfo->driver_info;
 }
 
